<!--Post: 7466--><!--Time: 1108508604-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7466"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 3:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve seen alot of speculation regarding whether the semen found at BTK&#39;s murder locations was actually his or whether he might have &#34;planted&#34; some that wasnt his own.  I&#39;ve also thought that maybe he made the male victims masterbate themselves.  However, has anyone looking into the chain-of-custody of the semen samples??? perhaps, someone &#40;BTK&#41; switched semen samples sometime between collection and analysis. ive done alot of work in environmental sampling and these days samples are kept under strict chain-of-custody for legal purposes. i dont know if they did so back then, but it might be worth trying to track down all those who could have had access to the semen samples. or has this been done?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7466-->
<!--Post: 7517--><!--Time: 1108540249-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7517"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 11:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not sure , in 1974 and during BTK main years of activity,if the police were aware of the significance of the semen samples or not. I seem to recall that they did some kind of comparison back then, but it seems like DNA tracing has been around forever and I can&#39;t think of anything they could compare.  <BR> <BR>I have read that the department have kept it under &#34;the proper conditions&#34; which I would assume would be frozen. Artificial insemenation has been around forever so that technology was well known.  <BR> <BR>He could have paid a prostitute to collect some semen for him with a story like &#34;I&#39;m sterile and dont want my wife to know...i&#39;ll pay you xxx$ to toss the condoms from your customers in a cooler &#40;dry ice&#41; or freezer and keep it for me&#34;. <BR> <BR>How well it tests DNA-wise after being in a condom, flung, scraped, frozen, kept for years in storage, I wouldn&#39;t know. Plus there is the human element about how well it was tagged treated etc, etc..  <BR> <BR>But, on the History Channel I saw them checking for matches using a DNA sample from inside the tooth of a 16th century skull. so...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7517-->
<!--Post: 7523--><!--Time: 1108551850-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7523"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:newmilleniumwriter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 3:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have to wonder when they even obtained the DNA.  By the time Wegerly was killed, they should have started testing - but she was not linked to the other known BTK killings.  No semen at that scene, I&#39;ve heard, but what about scrapings from under nails? <BR> <BR>I have a sinking feeling that no DNA still exists from the Otero, Vian or Fox killings.  If they have any from Wegerly - that is why it was never linked, although the killings were strikingly similar.   <BR> <BR>Supposedly, they obtained DNA from the first letter he sent last year.  If that is what they are swabbing against...what a farce. <BR> <BR>Younger people are starting to be swabbed - an indication that there is at least some thought that BTK is dead and a younger person is now hoaxing with his stash. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7523-->
<!--Post: 7626--><!--Time: 1108610666-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7626"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 7:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the police have no DNA from BTK, then why &#40;or how?&#41; was Mr. V. cleared because his DNA was a non-match with BTK&#39;s a couple of months ago? <BR> <BR>I believe the police have DNA from BTK. If not, it will require an enormous miracle to even learn BTK&#39;s identity let alone capture him. <BR> <BR>Prior to DNA testing, semen was still collected and stored. At least, that&#39;s what good police departments did.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7626-->
<!--Post: 7839--><!--Time: 1108707411-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7839"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This isn&#39;t much, but you can take it for what it&#39;s worth.  I heard a good rumor &#40;excellent &#34;chain of custody&#34;, so to speak&#41; that when asked somewhat privately about the quality of the DNA evidence, a member of LE stated that it was &#34;VERY good&#34; &#40;LE&#39;s emphasis&#41;.  Again, could just be propaganda, but the person who heard it believed that LE was not bluffing.  And no info on how much, where it was from, or if it was consistent over time.  Just that it was very good.  Sorry that I don&#39;t have any more than that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7839-->
<!--Post: 7967--><!--Time: 1108768672-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7967"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 3:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There are several samples of semen from different BTK crimes. All match as one &#40;same&#41;. This is what WPD is testing against.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7967-->
<!--Post: 8096--><!--Time: 1108871179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8096"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 7:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->thats very good to know... im sure im just being overly skeptical. however, i think that if i was BTK and i was in a position to be alone with the samples after/during collection and/or prior to or during analysis, that i could make them all match by switching them to a common source that wasn&#39;t mine... i say that it would still be prudent to exclude EVERYONE that may have had access to the samples... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8096-->
<!--Post: 8298--><!--Time: 1109041569-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8298"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 7:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->okay, before DNA, you could at least type blood an other fluids.It may not have pointed to a specific person, but rather narrowed it down. <BR>BTW, if semen is frozen, you can tell by the cellular structure and sometimes the tail...improperly stored &#40; like in a grocery bag in your fridge&#41; semen can be easily damaged.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8298-->
